e story.','The release of a new album','The launch of a celebrity’s restaurant.','What is planned for December?'),(347,'Its record-breaking sales','Its roots in Manchester.','Its focus on fiction and poetry.','Its broad range of authors.','What does Frederick Bissett emphasize about Tillford Exalt?'),(348,'Some new employees are absent.','Some boxes are incorrectly labeled.','A package delivery is delayed.','An access door is malfunctioning.','What problem does Mr. Skagen mention?'),(349,'An electrician has arrived at a work site.','Some equipment is operating smoothly.','Trainees can help with some shipments.','Ms. Sadauskas is well suited for her job.','At 9:02 A.M., what does Mr. Skagen most likely mean when he writes, “Yes, that works”?'),(350,'An image is not displaying clearly.','A projector needs to be set up.','Audio is not functioning properly.','A microphone needs to be repaired.','Why was the form submitted?'),(351,'Visit a client site','Deliver a product','Create an online video','Give a presentation','What is Ms. Deckow planning to do next week?'),(352,'2:00','2:15','2:30','3:00','At what time will the executive board meeting begin?'),(353,'Marketing','Finance','Advertising','Executive management','In what area does Mr. Iverman most likely work?'),(354,'To summarize a previous meeting','To explain a promotional campaign','To provide information about a budget','To review recently approved documents','Why does Ms. Glatt want a colleague to attend a meeting?'),(355,'She accepts Mr. Seidal’s offer.','She agrees that Mr. Iverman should attend the meeting at 3:00','She is pleased with the proposed budget.','She is happy that a project has been completed.','At 11:43 A.M., what does Ms. Glatt most likely mean when she writes, \'\'Sounds great”?'),(356,'He informed her of a job opening.','He will require a professional reference.','He would make a good business partner.','He is considering resigning from his position.','What does Ms. McFarland mention about Mr. Wilkins?'),(357,'transport','communicate','recommend','adapt','The word “convey” in paragraph 1, line 5, is closest in meaning to'),(358,'She wants a higher salary for her efforts.','She wants to work with a more experienced team.','She wants more opportunities for advancement.','She wants a role that inspires her more.','Why does Ms. McFarland want to leave her current position?'),(359,'To request a placement in a particular country.','To discuss how she came to acquire strategic industry contacts.','To explain how she became aware of certain world issues.','To emphasize her experience with people of different backgrounds.','Why does Ms. McFarland mention her travels?'),(360,'Medical supplies.','Farming equipment.','Cabinets and furniture.','Glass laboratory equipment.','What does Trexdale Supply make?'),(361,'It reorganized a client’s laboratory.','It converted its vehicles to use biofuels.','It expanded staffing at its production facility.','It helped a client organize a trade show.','What did Trexdale Supply do in a recent project?'),(362,'By e-mail','By phone','By instant message','By an online form','What method of communicating with Trexdale Supply is mentioned?'),(363,'Cook','Cashier','Interior designer','Event planner','What work experience would best qualify a candidate for the position?'),(364,'Respond to a survey','Arrange for an interview','Submit a recording','Provide references','According to the advertisement, what should people interested in applying do next?'),(365,'[1]','[2]','[3]','[4]','In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3], and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “Many of the world’s best-known brands rely on our product demonstrators to generate positive impressions of their products.”'),(366,'To promote a technology show','To introduce a product','To interview smartphone users','To announce a recall of a device','What is the purpose of the article?'),(367,'£39','£59','£79','£100','How much do the Gorman Pro Phone 4 wireless headphones cost?'),(368,'The screen size','The camera resolution','The price','The charger','What does the Pro Phone 4 have in common with prior models?'),(369,'[1]','[2]','[3]','[4]','In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3], and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “These upgrades do come at a cost.”'),(370,'It provides mobile phones to some employees.','Its employees value confidentiality.','It has recently changed its phone system.','It offers technology training to employees.','What does Ms. Xi’s request indicate about the company?'),(371,'periodic','orderly','customary','legitimate','In the e-mail, the word \'\'regular” in paragraph 1, line 6, is closest in meaning to'),(372,'In a weekly managers’ meeting','In a work order','In a phone call','In a personal voice mail','Where did Mr. Arnold learn about the details of Ms. Xi’s request?'),(373,'By agreeing to everything Ms. Xi asked for.','By resetting the password on Ms. Xi’s phone.','By referring the matter to another technician.','By proposing to fulfill only part of Ms. Xi’s request.','How does Mr. Arnold try to satisfy Ms. Xi\'s request?'),(374,'Make the needed changes to her voice-mail system.','Attend training about the new voice-mail system.','Confirm that she wants him to change her voice-mail system.','Provide a clear description of the problem with her voice-mail system.','What does Mr. Arnold ask Ms. Xi to do?'),(375,'He coordinates a game development team.','He is convinced that Titan Adventure is overpriced.','He is a new employee at Rimerko Games.','He will leave on a business trip on October 10.','In the e-mail, what is suggested about Mr. Merson?'),(376,'It is a major competitor of Titan Adventure.','It features an open-world format.','It is the first video game in a series.','It is Rimerko’s most challenging game.','In the review, what is indicated about Neptune’s Voyage ?'),(377,'She wrote the script for Neptune’s Voyage.','She successfully addressed Mr. Merson’s concern.','She won an award for game design.','She is a project manager.','What can be concluded about Ms. Hanshu?'),(378,'It has players act in the role of Neptune.','It uses lighting to show players where to navigate.','It introduces a completely new set of characters.','It lets players explore new features without guidance.','What does Mr. Weber find exciting about Neptune’s Voyage 7?'),(379,'On September 4','On October 10','On April 1','On May 5','When will Neptune’s Voyage be available?'),(380,'The advertising manager at a radio station.','The host of a community news program.','The music director at Wonder Ridge Radio.','The host of a sports radio program.','According to the schedule, who is Ms. Jones?'),(381,'To express praise for the radio station.','To ask about job opportunities.','To request more sports talk show programming.','To inquire about the name of a song.','What is the purpose of the e-mail?'),(382,'Between 6 and noon.','Between noon and 4','Between 4 and 7','Between 7 and 10','When did Mr. Fabre most likely first listen to Wonder Ridge Radio?'),(383,'A willingness to travel.','Familiarity with computers.','A degree in communications.','Extensive experience in the radio industry.','What does the job advertisement suggest applicants must have?'),(384,'Coffee Break','Afternoon Jazz','Folk Frenzy','Josie\'s Joint','What radio program will probably receive the most support from the programming assistant?'),(385,'They can be made only on certain days.','They can be made only online.','They can be filed only by authorized personnel.','They can be filed only after a fee is paid.','What do the instructions indicate about records requests?'),(386,'To add information to a Web portal','To help his company advise the city','To identify an accounting error','To learn how an agency is structured','According to the e-mail, how does Mr. Brandenberg plan to use some public information?'),(387,'Go through a security screening.','Get a parking permit.','Present some identification.','Sign a logbook.','What does the sign indicate visitors must do before entering a building?'),(388,'An itemized statement of fees.','A letter from his company.','A phone call from a city official.','A password for the Web portal.','What was Mr. Brandenberg expecting to receive?'),(389,'Room 100','Room 101','Room 102','Room 103','What room will Mr. Brandenberg most likely visit?'),(390,'He enjoys his work as a director.','He has been a mentor to many young people.','He is a well-known actor.','He has written many books.','What does the review mention about Mr. Eklund?'),(391,'In Sweden','In France','In Italy','In the United Kingdom','Where most likely will Ms. Joshi meet Mr. Eklund?'),(392,'To go on a vacation','To interview for a new job','To attend an international film festival','To speak at a conference','According to the first e-mail, what is one reason Ms. Joshi will travel in April?'),(393,'To reserve a hotel room','To confirm meeting arrangements','To discuss an idea for a movie','To ask for transportation','What is the purpose of the second e-mail?'),(394,'He hopes to write for a British news site.','He just hired a new assistant.','He was pleased with Ms. Joshi’s review of his book.','He frequently cooks special meals.','What can be concluded about Mr. Eklund?'),(437,'To rent a facility','To hire a photographer','To request a price list','To schedule a repair','Why is the man calling?'),(438,'What problem does the woman mention?','Her service does not cover sports events.','The weather will be bad on Tuesday.','The time the man requested is too late.','What problem does the woman mention?'),(439,'23123','12312312','12321','123123','1212'),(440,'1','1','1','1','1'),(441,'1','1','1','1','1');
